  <h2 id="completion">The completion-rate reality nobody puts on the brochure</h2>

  <p>
    Distance and online credit-bearing programs, studied across university systems worldwide, show
    meaningfully higher attrition than in-person, full-time study — commonly cited in the 30-50%
    range for credit-bearing distance and online courses generally, well above typical on-campus
    dropout levels. India-specific per-university completion data is not consistently published,
    but the underlying pattern holds here too: the biggest risk to a distance MBA is not the exam
    difficulty, it is losing momentum somewhere around month eight or nine when work gets busy and
    the flexible deadline quietly becomes no deadline at all.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--amber">
    <p>
      Before you enrol, be honest about your own track record with self-paced commitments —
      unfinished online courses, gym memberships, side projects. A distance MBA removes the
      external structure of a classroom and a cohort schedule almost entirely. If structure, not
      motivation, is usually your bottleneck, budget for that risk before you pay the fee, not after
      you fall behind.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="checkpoint">Use The 4-Checkpoint Protocol before you enrol</h2>

  <p>
    A low fee and a familiar university name cannot tell you whether a distance MBA fits your
    specific situation. The 4-Checkpoint Protocol narrows the decision to what actually matters.
  </p>

  <div class="protocol-stack">
    {checkpointItems.map((item) => (
      <div class="checkpoint">
